From 45b64065de6a271c2e91dd51f25eaaf22035f1f6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 21 Aug 2026 10:52:24 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/3] fix(workspace): the toolbar above the page wrapped
 everywhere except where it had to
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Found by measuring the deployed site at a true 390 px layout rather than under
mobile emulation, which hides this: Chrome answers an overflowing page by
widening its own layout viewport, so the earlier check compared 609 against 609
and passed. At 390 the document really does scroll sideways in Annotate, and
the whole app is then drawn at about 64 %.

The cause is one missing utility. Seven panes carry the same toolbar row above
the page; the organize one has always had `flex-wrap` and the other six never
did. Annotate's row needs 609 px — 445 of it before this session added Undo and
Redo to it, so the row was already over a phone's width and the new buttons
made it plainly so.

Wrapping rather than scrolling, because these rows end in Save: a primary
action must not sit off an edge nobody knows to drag. The workspace bar stays
the deliberate exception — nine mode buttons wrapped would push the page down
on every screen, so that one scrolls.

Measured after: all nine modes report `documentElement.scrollWidth === 390` at
a 390 px layout.

Design contract §3 records the rule and the exception.

