From afc6ce9bc3e6f22ec3a58e995baabbafb60da3b2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 21 Aug 2026 10:52:24 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/3] fix(workspace): "Organize pages" now opens the page grid
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Two halves of one gap, neither of which shows up until you look for it.

`tool-page.ts` maps each interactive tool to the mode it exists for, and
`organize` was the single entry with an empty object — so `/organize-pdf`, the
tool whose entire subject is the page grid, dropped the visitor into the
reading view with the grid one unexplained click away.

Setting the mode was not enough: the workspace's query-param handler accepted
seven modes and `organize` was not among them (nor `view`), so the URL said
`?mode=organize` and the reading view rendered anyway. That is presumably why
the map was left empty in the first place. Both are fixed together, because
either alone is a no-op.

The new spec asserts the landing mode for all eight interactive tools, not just
the one that was wrong — the same omission could be made again in any of them.

