The deploy did what it set out to do, proved against the live site rather than
against the report of it: identity by reproducing production's bundle hashes
byte for byte, the viewer by sampling canvas pixels, the cache rule by watching
a deliberately-cached page raster keep its max-age, and every round trip by
reading the resulting PDF back with a second library.

Two checks failed. One is a regression this branch fixes; the other is
pre-existing. Both were invisible to looking and only appeared under
measurement — the phone overflow in particular passed its previous check
because Chrome hides an overflow by widening its own layout viewport, so the
check compared 609 against 609.

One earlier finding is withdrawn on live evidence: `separate` extraction works
in production; the e2e failure is in the harness. That queue row is re-scoped
to the test.

